course: dictionary
lesson: 14055
title: Marshals: one word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Marshals» can be a noun, meaning people with a job, or a verb, meaning to organise. Read the words around it to find out which one fits.
explain: «The race marshals in bright yellow jackets waved the runners on.» Race marshals are officials who organise people at a race and keep them safe, so marshals is a noun here.
explain: «She marshals her thoughts before she writes her essay.» Marshals is a verb here: she gathers and organises her thoughts. Check by swapping in organises. The sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: «Marshals» can be a plural noun, meaning more than one marshal.
fact: A marshal is an official who organises people at an event, such as a race, parade or festival, and keeps them safe.
fact: In Western stories, a town marshal is like a sheriff, keeping law and order.
fact: A field marshal is a very high-ranking army or air-force officer.
fact: «Marshals» can also be a verb, meaning gathers and organises people or things, such as ideas.
exercise: «The marshals in high-vis jackets guided the runners to the start line.» Who are the marshals? | Old castles on a hill | *People who organise an event and keep people safe | Runners who won the race | Cars that drive very fast
exercise: «Ben marshals his ideas into three clear paragraphs.» What does marshals mean here? | Shouts loudly | Throws away | Forgets | *Gathers and organises
exercise: In a Western story, a town marshal is a bit like whom? | A cook at a feast | *A sheriff who keeps law and order | A teacher | A rainbow
test: «The field marshal led the army across the valley.» What is a field marshal? | A type of tree | A runner in a race | *A very high-ranking army officer
test: «Mia marshalled the children into a line for the bus.» What does marshalled mean? | *Gathered and organised | Scattered | Lost | Hid
exam: «The festival marshals kept the crowds safe at the gate.» What are the marshals? | *Officials who organise people and keep them safe | Musicians playing in the park | Wizards who cast spells | Dogs trained to find food
